Description:
White Russian kale is a dark green, oak leaf-shaped kale with white stems that's great for cooking or eating raw. It's a popular variety that's disease resistant and has a sweet flavor that intensifies when cooked. Here are some more characteristics of White Russian kale:&nbsp;
Taste:White Russian kale has a crisp, sweet flavor that's considered by many to be the best tasting. Frost improves the flavor even more.&nbsp;
Appearance:White Russian kale has lightly frilled leaves with white veins and a gray-green base
Preparation:White Russian kale can be blanched and used in soups, stews, casseroles, and side dishes.
